      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:10owam3'
    '|a||And it falls as you slide down the curve. The falling rate is the bend.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:wrqsyp'
    '|b||Another way to see it: draw a straight line between two lopsided bundles. Its middle, ten and ten, lies beyond her curve.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7320
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:2wd48w'
    '|a||So she''d rather have a mix than a pile of either. That''s all the bend says.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:llc4ht'
    '|a||There is a one-line formula behind that slide. Show the math, or skip it?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5960
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||The steepness of the curve at any point is her hats divided by her shoes, for this curve.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6840
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||At two pairs and eighteen hats, that''s nine hats for a tiny step more of shoes.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5440
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1wj1y15'
    '|a||At twelve pairs and three hats, a quarter. The ratio falls as you slide, and that''s the bend.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1u3629f'
    '|a||So a bent curve means a mix beats a pile. Does every taste bend like that?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6360
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Take left shoes and right shoes. A third left shoe, with only two right ones, is worth nothing to you.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5920
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:psojgz'
    '|a||So her curves have corners. The goods only count in pairs: economists call them perfect complements.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1qret8p'
    '|b||Now the opposite: two brands of eggs she can''t tell apart.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3800
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:ue6bo3'
    '|a||She swaps one for one, anywhere. The swap rate never falls, so the line never bends: perfect substitutes.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:lgk5zj'
    '|b||And hats and shoes sit in between. Bent, but no corner.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4200
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:o5mgnj'
    '|a||Your turn: put each pair of goods under the shape you''d expect for most people.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:f7dk3'
    '|b||So the shape is the taste. It says how easily one thing can stand in for another.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5680
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||Hold on. Thurstone''s subject never got a single hat. He only said what he''d pick.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4960
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||That was exactly the complaint. In 1942 Allen Wallis and Milton Friedman wrote that a satisfactory experiment needs actual reactions to actual stimuli.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:gel2t1'
    '|b||Answers about made-up bundles, they said, don''t satisfy that.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4400
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1et8z1i'
    '|a||So later experimenters made the choices real. In 1969, Kenneth MacCrimmon and Masanao Toda offered cash and French pastries, and the pastries had to be eaten in the lab.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:jdbb0b'
    '|b||So how sure are we about the bend?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2960
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1k5dhnj'
    '|a||For ordinary goods, mostly agreed: most people spread their money over many things instead of piling up one. Measuring one person''s whole map is still hard.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1s6svx1'
    '|b||Three questions on new cases. Sara is torn between 2 teas + 8 biscuits and 8 teas + 2 biscuits. Her curves bend the usual way. Now she''s offered 6 teas + 6 biscuits. What does she do?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13880
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:nwwhix'
    '|b||Takes 6 + 6. A bent curve puts the halfway mix, 5 + 5, at least level with her two bundles, and 6 + 6 is more of both.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10080
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||Ola has twenty coffees and one croissant a week; Kari has five of each. Same tastes. Who would give up more coffees for one more croissant?':
